# Scaffolding prompt: knowledge architecture for [PROJECT_NAME]

## Assignment

Stand up the three-tier knowledge architecture described in
[TRELLIS_LOCATION]`/principles/01-knowledge-architecture.md` in this repository. Read that file
first if you haven't already — this prompt is the concrete checklist for applying it, not a
replacement for understanding why it's structured this way.

- **Permanent project knowledge lives in:** `[dir, e.g. docs/]`
- **Permanent process knowledge lives in:** `[dir, e.g. .ai/ or process/]`
- **Disposable per-role scratch lives in:** `[dir, e.g. .work/ or .scratch/]`
- **Entry-point file:** `[filename, e.g. AGENTS.md]` at the repository root

## Steps

1. **Inventory what already exists.** Do not assume an empty repository. List any existing
   documentation, ad hoc notes, config, or structure that already occupies these paths or serves
   a similar purpose. If this repository already has its own documentation conventions, note the
   overlap explicitly rather than silently colliding with it.
2. **Create the three tiers**, if they don't already exist. **Preserve everything already
   present** — this is additive scaffolding, not a rewrite. Where existing content clearly
   belongs in one of the new tiers (e.g. an existing architecture doc belongs under permanent
   project knowledge), move or reference it deliberately and say so in your summary; don't leave
   duplicate copies in two places.
3. **Create or update the entry-point file** using
   [TRELLIS_LOCATION]`/templates/AGENTS.md.template`. Keep it concise: it routes to the tiers
   above, in the order they should be read, and contains no detailed project knowledge itself.
   If one already exists, integrate rather than replace — preserve anything in it that's still
   accurate.
4. **Add a short index/README at the root of each tier** stating what it answers and what
   belongs in it (see [TRELLIS_LOCATION]`/templates/docs-index-README.md.template` for the
   permanent-project-knowledge tier as a starting point; the process-knowledge and scratch tiers
   need only a few sentences each).
5. **Update this repository's ignore rules** (`.gitignore` or equivalent) so the scratch tier
   (and any cache/log subdirectories under it) is excluded from version control, **except** the
   index/README files created in step 4 — those should stay tracked so the tier's purpose is
   documented even though its contents aren't.
6. **Do not** create role prompts, standards, or workflow documents in this pass — that's a
   separate, deliberate step (see [TRELLIS_LOCATION]`/templates/starter-prompt.md.template` Part
   2 or `ADOPTING.md`), and mixing it into pure structural scaffolding makes both harder to
   review.

## Before reporting, verify

- [ ] All three tiers exist at the paths specified above.
- [ ] The entry-point file is concise, routes to the tiers, and contains no detailed content of
      its own.
- [ ] Each tier's purpose is unambiguous — a new reader could tell, from the index files alone,
      which tier a given piece of knowledge belongs in.
- [ ] Ignore rules exclude the scratch tier's working content, but its index/README stays
      tracked.
- [ ] Nothing that existed before this pass was deleted or silently overwritten — anything moved,
      merged, or superseded is called out explicitly in the summary below.
- [ ] No temporary or scratch directory is referenced as a dependency anywhere (build config,
      other docs, code).
- [ ] **No existing project behavior changed.** This pass adds structure for documentation and
      process knowledge; it does not touch application code, build output, or runtime behavior.
      If anything outside the tiers above and the entry-point file was modified, that's a signal
      this step overran its scope — undo it or justify it explicitly.

## Report

Summarize every change made: files and directories created, files modified (and what changed),
anything preserved or merged rather than overwritten, and anything flagged for human follow-up
(e.g. an existing doc whose right home wasn't obvious).
